### NITKSAA Event — Payment API Examples
### Live-verified against a local dev instance (APP_ENV=development) on 2026-08-22.
### @baseUrl and @token are placeholders — see PAYMENT_API_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md for how a
### backend access token is minted (POST /api/v1/auth/firebase after a real Firebase login;
### dev-only test identities use app.middleware.auth.make_access_token directly).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_TOKEN
@adminToken = REPLACE_WITH_PLATFORM_ADMIN_BEARER_TOKEN

### 1. Server-computed pricing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/14760/payment-pricing
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected 200:
# {
#   "event_id": 14760, "configuration_key": "doc-DOC1787411618", "currency": "INR",
#   "base_amount": "100.00", "gst_enabled": true, "gst_rate": "18.00", "gst_mode": "exclusive",
#   "tax_amount": "18.00", "convenience_fee_enabled": false, "convenience_fee": "0.00",
#   "final_amount": "118.00",
#   "line_items": [
#     {"label": "Registration fee", "amount": "100.00"},
#     {"label": "GST (18.00%)", "amount": "18.00"}
#   ]
# }

### 2. Register (paid event -> seat_held)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/14760/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"attendee_note": "doc verification"}

### Expected 201: {"registration_id": 5665, "status": "seat_held", "hold_expires_at": "...", ...}

### 3. Create payment order (idempotent on idempotency_key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/registrations/5665/payment-order
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idempotency_key": "client-generated-uuid-001"}

### Expected 201:
# {
#   "order_id": "ORD-IinxJRey-TyC", "registration_id": 5665, "event_id": 14760,
#   "currency": "INR", "base_amount": "100.00", "tax_amount": "18.00",
#   "convenience_fee": "0.00", "final_amount": "118.00", "amount_paid": "0.00",
#   "outstanding_amount": "118.00", "status": "created", "registration_status": "payment_pending",
#   "expires_at": "2026-08-22T15:29:04.156142Z", "can_pay": true, "can_retry": true,
#   "safe_message": "Complete payment to confirm your registration."
# }

### 3b. Repeat with the SAME idempotency_key -> same order, still 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/registrations/5665/payment-order
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"idempotency_key": "client-generated-uuid-001"}

### 4. Create a payment attempt (sandbox SUCCESS)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-orders/ORD-IinxJRey-TyC/attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"scenario": "SUCCESS"}

### Expected 201 (already resolved — sandbox webhook processed synchronously):
# {
#   "attempt_id": "ATT-sMWzjpgVOm6t", "order_id": "ORD-IinxJRey-TyC", "attempt_number": 1,
#   "gateway": "deterministic_sandbox", "status": "captured", "scenario": "SUCCESS",
#   "initiated_at": "2026-08-22T15:14:04.252047Z"
# }

### 5. Get order after capture
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-orders/ORD-IinxJRey-TyC
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected 200: status=paid, registration_status=registered, amount_paid=118.00, can_pay=false

### 6. Attendee-safe timeline
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-orders/ORD-IinxJRey-TyC/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected 200: 5 entries with friendly `label`s (Seat reserved / Payment order created /
### Payment started / Payment successful / Registration confirmed)

### 7. Failure -> retry -> success
# POST .../attempts {"scenario":"FAILURE"}  -> 201 status=failed
# GET  .../payment-orders/{id}              -> registration_status=payment_failed, can_retry=true
# POST .../attempts {"scenario":"SUCCESS"}  -> 201 attempt_number=2, status=captured
# POST .../attempts {"scenario":"SUCCESS"}  -> 409 payment_order_not_payable (terminal order)

### 8. Pending -> verification
# POST .../attempts {"scenario":"PENDING"}        -> 201 status=pending
# GET  .../payment-orders/{id}                    -> registration_status=payment_verification,
#                                                     can_retry=false
# POST .../payment-attempts/{id}/verify           -> 200 status=pending (checked promptly)

### 9. Cross-user denial (different bearer token against someone else's order)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-orders/ORD-IinxJRey-TyC
Authorization: Bearer {{OTHER_USERS_TOKEN}}

### Expected 404: {"detail": "payment_order_not_found"}

### 10. Unauthenticated request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/14760/payment-pricing

### Expected 403: {"detail": "Not authenticated"}

### 11. Webhook: unknown gateway
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-gateways/fake_gateway/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
X-Sandbox-Signature: bogus

{}

### Expected 404: {"detail": "unknown_gateway"}

### 12. Webhook: invalid signature
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/payment-gateways/deterministic_sandbox/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
X-Sandbox-Signature: bogus

{"event_id": "some-unique-uuid", "event_type": "payment.captured", "gateway_order_ref": "sbx_ord_x", "amount": "1.00", "currency": "INR", "issued_at": 9999999999}

### Expected 200: {"status": "rejected", "processing_status": "rejected"}
### (signature is checked before the timestamp gate, so this is rejected on signature, not "future_skew")

### 13. Admin: gateway registry config (requires platform_admin/finance_operator/auditor/support)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/payments/gateway-config
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected 200:
# {
#   "environment": "development", "configured_gateway_mode": "deterministic_sandbox",
#   "active_gateway": "deterministic_sandbox",
#   "gateways": [{
#     "name": "deterministic_sandbox", "enabled": true,
#     "capabilities": ["create_payment", "process_webhook", "verify_webhook"],
#     "supported_scenarios": ["CANCELLED", "DELAYED_FAILURE", "DELAYED_SUCCESS", "FAILURE", "PENDING", "SUCCESS"]
#   }]
# }
### No secrets in this payload (payment_sandbox_signing_secret is never returned).

### 14. Admin: gateway registry config without a qualifying role -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/payments/gateway-config
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected 403: {"detail": "payment_role_required"}

### 15. Admin: WP1 config lifecycle — create draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/events/14760/payment-configurations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "configuration_key": "doc-draft-verify",
  "base_amount": "200.00",
  "gst_enabled": true,
  "gst_rate": "18.00",
  "gst_mode": "exclusive",
  "seat_hold_minutes": 15,
  "payment_session_expiry_minutes": 15
}

### Expected 201: {"configuration_id": ..., "status": "draft", ...}

### 16. Admin: validate draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/events/14760/payment-configurations/{{configId}}/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected 200: {"configuration_id": ..., "valid": true, "errors": []}

### 17. Admin: publish draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/events/14760/payment-configurations/{{configId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected 200: status="published"; the event's previously-published config row is retired
### in the same transaction.

### 18. Admin: publish again on an already-published config -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/events/14760/payment-configurations/{{configId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected 409: {"detail": "payment_configuration_not_a_draft"}

### 19. Admin: explicit expiry sweep (platform_admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/payments/lifecycle/expire-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected 200: {"expired_count": 0, "expired_order_ids": []}  (when nothing is eligible)

### 20. Dev diagnostics: resolve a stuck pending attempt (development env only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/diagnostics/payments/attempts/{{attemptId}}/resolve
X-Dev-User: admin
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "SUCCESS"}

### Expected 200: {"status":"ok","processing_status":"processed","order_status":"paid",
###                "registration_status":"registered", ...}
